<title>UK: Celltech sees septic shock results early Q2.</title>
<headline>Celltech sees septic shock results early Q2.</headline>
<byline>Jonathan Birt</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drug discovery company Celltech Group Plc said on Tuesday that keenly-awaited results of late stage trials of its septic shock drug will be published early in the second quarter.</p>
<p>The company hopes that the drug, which is being developed jointly with Germany's Bayer AG, will be the first successful treatment of septic shock following a string of high-profile failures by rival products. Septic shock is a poisoning of the body which often sets in after surgery.</p>
</text>
